pkgmk.conf(5)									      pkgmk.conf(5)

NAME
     pkgmk.conf - Configuration file for pkgmk.

DESCRIPTION
     pkgmk.conf configures pkgutils package make, pkgmk(8).

FILE FORMAT
     The  file	consists of a number of variable assignments of the form option=value. Comments can
     be specified by putting a hash (#) symbol as the first character on the line.

DIRECTIVES
     If some option is not used (commented out or not included in the configuration  file  at  all)
     pkgmk will take a default action.

     export CFLAGS=’STRING’
	    Set C compiler options.
	    Default: none

     export CXXFLAGS=’STRING’
	    Set C++ compiler options.
	    Default: none

     export JOBS=’NUMBER’
	    Set the number of commands to run simultaneously when building a port.
	    Default: none

     export MAKEFLAGS=’STRING’
	    Set make options.
	    Default: none

     PKGMK_SOURCE_MIRRORS=(’STRING’)
	    Set mirrors to check and download source archives from.
	    Default: none

     PKGMK_SOURCE_DIR=’STRING’
	    Set directory for downloaded source archives.
	    Default: directory of Pkgfile.

     PKGMK_PACKAGE_DIR=’STRING’
	    Set directory for built packages.
	    Default: directory of Pkgfile.

     PKGMK_WORK_DIR=’STRING’
	    Set directory for building packages.
	    Default: ’foo/work’, where foo is the directory of the Pkgfile.

     PKGMK_DOWNLOAD_PROG=’STRING’
	    Use specified program to download source archives. Valid strings are curl and wget.
	    Default: ’curl’

     PKGMK_CURL_OPTS=’STRING’
	    Additional options for curl(1), which is used by pkgmk to download all files.

     PKGMK_WGET_OPTS=’STRING’
	    Additional options for wget(1), which is used by pkgmk to download all files.

     PKGMK_DOWNLOAD=’STRING’
	    If set to ’yes’, pkgmk will download the source archives if necessary.
	    Default: ’no’

     PKGMK_IGNORE_FOOTPRINT=’STRING’
	    If set to ’yes’, pkgmk will not perform a footprint check of the built package.
	    Default: ’no’

     PKGMK_IGNORE_NEW=’STRING’
	    If set to ’yes’, pkgmk will ignore new files in a footprint mismatch.
	    Default: ’no’

     PKGMK_NO_STRIP=’STRING’
	    If set to ’no’, pkgmk will strip built binaries.
	    Default: ’no’

     PKGMK_COMPRESSION_MODE=’STRING’
	    Option to select the mode used to compress the packages. Valid strings are gz, bz2, xz,
	    lz, and zst.
	    Default: ’gz’

SEE ALSO
     pkgmk(8)

